{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe mean reversion lag: The model consistently fails to anticipate sharp downward corrections following price spikes (e.g., the drop from ~90 to ~76), maintaining a persistent upward drift bias. Apply a negative correction factor immediately after any 3-day price increase exceeding 2%.",
    "Adjust for sentiment disconnect: The model ignores negative sentiment signals (e.g., -0.25) and positive spikes (e.g., +0.20), treating them as noise. When sentiment history contains a negative value, reduce the forecast by 3-5% to account for the model's failure to price in bearish sentiment.",
    "Cap long-term horizon optimism: Forecasts beyond day 10 systematically overshoot the eventual equilibrium, predicting a steady rise while the true outcome stabilizes or declines. Flatten the forecast slope after day 10 to match the observed volatility range rather than the model's linear trend.",
    "Implement spike-reversion trigger: Upon observing a true outcome spike (e.g., >88), immediately truncate the subsequent 5-day forecast to prevent the model from projecting further gains, as the market historically reverts to the 76-80 range within 10 days."
  ]
}
